SPF_MAX_MECH_LEN/SPF_MAX_MOD_LEN (511) were checked against the whole
compiled record, so mechanisms past ~511 bytes (64 ip4) were silently
dropped, -all included, and compilation reported no error. Mechanisms
past the new limits are a permerror; modifiers past them are skipped
with a warning, as RFC 7208 6 requires unknown ones to be ignored.
https://github.com/shevek/libspf2/issues/21
https://github.com/shevek/libspf2/issues/48
https://github.com/shevek/libspf2/issues/60

